# Rovas work for Rovas agents

When Civic needs **Rovas-side** changes (new/changed Services resources, OAuth,
Drupal rules, `/rovas/*` payloads, claim registry, deploy notes for rovdev):

1. **Write the task for the Rovas agent** under
   `~/Documents/homeProjects/rovas/docs/integration/` — that tree is the source
   of truth for agents working in the **rovas** repo:
   - Copy `civic_tasks/_template.md` → `civic_tasks/active/<slug>.md`
     (Product / Contract / Checklist / Smoke).
   - Add a row to the **Task directory** in
     [`civic.md`](file:///Users/sano/Documents/homeProjects/rovas/docs/integration/civic.md).
   - Do **not** append a new `## Next work` section to `civic.md` (legacy
     pattern; open work lives only under `civic_tasks/active/`).
2. Keep Civic-side notes in `docs/rovas-integration.md` (Expo + Civic API).
   Link the Rovas task slug; do not duplicate the full Rovas implementation
   checklist here.
3. Do **not** rely on chat history alone — if Rovas must build something, it
   must be written into the Rovas integration docs so a Rovas agent can pick
   it up without this conversation.

## Hard boundary — do not implement Rovas

**Civic agents must not implement, edit, or deploy Rovas application code**
(Drupal modules under `sites/all/modules/custom/`, Services wiring, update
hooks, PHP in the **rovas** repo, rovdev/prod deploys). That work belongs to
the **Rovas agent**, following the task file above.

Civic agents may only:

- Author/update the Rovas **task contract** and Task directory row
- Update Civic companion notes in `docs/rovas-integration.md`
- Implement **Civic** (Expo, `services/api`, `@civic/shared`) against that
  contract

If a request would require changing Rovas PHP or Drupal config, stop at the
docs/contract and leave implementation to the Rovas agent.
